A colleague informs about the inclusion of illegal Internet downloads in the criminal code:
A. The download of a song would be a violation of the law involving six months imprisonment.
However, if you rob a music business below a value of 400 euros, this is only considered a simple violation (Article 623.1).
If you rob the business up to a value of 1000 euros, then the theft is classified as a criminal offence, but the penalty is less than in the case of a download (Article 234 of the Criminal Code).
C. If you stole a car and return it forty hours later, then the penalty is still lower than for a download (Article 244.1).
D. It is less serious to participate in a brawl than in a music data exchange.
Participating in a rebellious altercation results in a prison sentence of three to 12 months (Article 154 of the Criminal Code), while the data-exchange results in a deprivation of imprisonment of six months up to two years
(Article 270 Penal Code).
According to Article 184.2 of the Criminal Code, sexual harassment in the workplace is considered less dire than downloading a DVD film from the internet.
F. Trading in copyright-protecteded films, the authorization of which has not taken place by authors, is subject to a higher penalty than the distribution of pornographic footage to minors (Article 186).
Well yes, so if my colleague should be right, then someone has screwed up his demands quite a bit.
